# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# ...except the documented template of which keys a deployment needs
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# amplify
#
# amplify/ is TRACKED. It was ignored while it held the untouched `npm create
# amplify` scaffold — a Todo model and a defineAuth that nothing deployed and
# nothing imported. It now holds the real backend definition, and Amplify
# Hosting builds from this repository, so a definition it cannot see is a
# definition that does not exist.
#
# What stays ignored is everything GENERATED from it: the sandbox's build
# directory and the outputs file, which carries deployment-specific endpoint
# ids and would conflict between one person's sandbox and the next.
.amplify
amplify_outputs*
amplifyconfiguration*
